# 0.7.1: /spawn = vanilla's own SpawnCommand (same name, sub-commands set / setdefault, usage variant <player>, index argument), with
# plain /spawn going to the Zone 1 landing while 'Zone 1 = server spawn' is on and a landing is set; everything else = super.execute.
# Vanilla's tree (HytaleServer.jar 0.7.1): /spawn = node spawn.self + group Builder, /spawn <player> = node spawn.other (inherits the
# Builder group), /spawn set = group WorldEditor, /spawn default = group Admin (auto nodes). /spawn + /spawn <player> become admin-only
# (HANDOFF section 3: own node + setPermissionGroups(new String[0]) - an explicit node never goes to a whole group); /spawn set and
# /spawn default keep vanilla's own groups.
# 0.7.2 (Skyy 2026-10-16 "/SPAWN FOR PLAYERS"): the top /spawn is OPEN (requireNoPermission in WgSpawnCmd's constructor - no node,
# every player); its groups stay [] (no node to hand out); the <player> variant keeps spawn.other + its explicit empty list; set /
# default keep vanilla's groups.
M(shome, r"""
public static int adminTop(Object c) {
  if (c == null) return 0;
  int n = 0;
  try {
    Class ac = Class.forName("@ACMD@");
    java.lang.reflect.Method m = ac.getDeclaredMethod("setPermissionGroups", new Class[] { Class.forName("[Ljava.lang.String;") });
    m.setAccessible(true);
    m.invoke(c, new Object[] { new String[0] });
    n++;
    java.lang.reflect.Field f = ac.getDeclaredField("variantCommands");
    f.setAccessible(true);
    Object v = f.get(c);
    if (v instanceof java.util.Map) {
      Object[] b = ((java.util.Map) v).values().toArray();
      for (int i = 0; i < b.length; i++) {
        m.invoke(b[i], new Object[] { new String[0] });
        n++;
      }
    }
  } catch (Throwable t) { @PKG@.WgLog.warn("/spawn: could not make /spawn and /spawn <player> admin-only (" + t + ")"); }
  return n;
}""")
